Comment hello.sim - Simula cli: Hello, World!
  WHAT: prints one line, Hello, World!, and stops.
  WHY:  it is the smallest complete Simula 67 program: one block between
        begin and end, and one output procedure from the Simula 67 Common
        Base (outtext prints text, outimage ends the line).
  Simula comments run from the word comment to the next semicolon, so
  this text must not contain a semicolon. Source for the convention and
  the procedures: Dahl, Myhrhaug, Nygaard, SIMULA 67 Common Base Language,
  Norwegian Computing Center, 1968 (report NR 743), sections "Comment
  conventions" and "outtext" (https://www.softwarepreservation.org/projects/ALGOL/manual/NR_report_743_Dahl_Myhrhaug_Nygaard_Simula-67-Common-Base-Language.pdf)
  and GNU Cim 5.1 implements that Common Base.;

begin
   comment outtext prints the text, with no line end yet;
   outtext("Hello, World!");
   comment outimage ends the line, like a newline in C or print in Python;
   outimage
end;
